From 9949356bc8ea4b8f31a083e4d3550f4fb507efcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ahmadsb101 <ahmadsb101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:54:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fifo: polled reads (empty() before read) in a stall
 pipeline do not freeze it

The read of 'if (!s.empty()) s.read()' is predicated on the poll, so an empty
input issues a bubble and the iterations in flight go on; only a full output
freezes the pipeline. The C trace never sees a failed poll, so the read was
treated as blocking, and every pipelined polling stage froze until its next
inputs came. SODA's forwarding chains then needed more items in flight than
its exactly sized FIFOs hold (LightningSim deadlocks on 5 of 11 as-generated
small designs, up to +185% on others).

Writes of such pipelines are anchored to their iteration's read like FRP
writes (anchor_delta), and a stalled one holds back the next stage of the
chain (anchor_freeze). LSIM_POLL=0 turns it off.

Small SODA set (11 as generated, 14 patched) and 30 microbenchmarks: all 0
or one mapping step (-8/-9 cycles) against cosim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
